Collapse the duplicated block queueing of the HVX flash attention (lab proposal)

flash_attn_ext_f16_thread compiles to 21472 bytes in one body, and on the phone
FLASH_ATTN_EXT shows IU_NO_PKT 11.0 %, the highest instruction-fetch stall of the pp512 profile
of the 4B. The row loop queued the K, V and mask transfer of a block from four places with the
body written out each time. This proposal moves that body into one function that stays out of
line, which removes three of the four copies. It changes no arithmetic, thus the output is
unchanged.

diff -urN a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.c b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.c
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.c	2026-09-20 02:59:51.925406487 +0300
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.c	2026-09-20 03:13:25.175925742 +0300
@@ -158,6 +158,25 @@
     dma_cache    m_cache;
